# Goal wrapping Flow = "verify loop + dynamic DAG". Each ATTEMPT runs a whole Flow, which
# at runtime GENERATES a dataflow DAG of agents for the task and runs the independent nodes
# in parallel (supervised BEAM processes); Goal's cheap checker then verifies the acceptance
# condition and, if unmet, runs a FRESH attempt (a newly generated DAG) with feedback, until
# met or the round cap. Goal itself composes nothing -- Flow does the dynamic composition;
# Goal is the verify-until-met layer on top.
#
# SLOW: a full Flow per round (a designer call + parallel nodes + a terminal node) + a check,
# so max_rounds is kept low. Local Ollama.
#   jet acp-serve acp_goal_flow_demo::Composer::handle examples/acp_goal_flow_demo.jet
# Try: "Compare three caching strategies for a read-heavy API and recommend one."
module acp_goal_flow_demo
  agent Composer
    runner Goal(accept: "compares at least three distinct options and ends with a clear, single recommendation",
                via: {name: :Flow},
                surface: true,
                max_rounds: 2,
                model: "ollama:qwen3.6:35b-a3b")
    ask handle(task)
  end
end
